claimed: intent-classify — intent classification as ONE Schema derivation: a hierarchical sum type IS the taxonomy, the FrameNet-style frame (Frame Elements = required product fields) and the parser of the model reply, so a label outside the enumeration is a decode error rather than a parsing bug. Two axes kept separate: multi-intent falls out of per-span detection, ambiguity is ranked alts within a span. One model tier only (Structured.cut stops generation at the closing brace); the symbolic (Postings/BM25) and vector (centroid/linear probe) tiers are deferred behind a measured trigger, and a fine-tuned encoder is refused (label cost, a JVM-only native runtime in a cross-built library, taxonomy churn). Eval is a streaming Aggregator giving per-class P/R/F1 at both levels plus an EXECUTABLE promotion rule (no class regresses more than two points), run over a Rerun journal so a prompt change replays deterministically. First step is a cheap measurement, not code: whether schema field order actually drives emission order, since the why-before-label vs why-after-label trade-off rests on it.
